<title>SOUTH KOREA: Asia Motors suspends July wage payment.</title>
<headline>Asia Motors suspends July wage payment.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asia Motors, a commercial vehicle producer within the battered Kia Group, has suspended its July wage payment, a group spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Today is the pay day for Asia Motors employees, but there will be no salary payment,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>He said many Asia Motors employees had voluntarily given up their July wages. He gave no further details.</p>
<p>Creditor banks decided to bail out Asia Motors and 17 other affiliates of the Kia Group, including Kia Motors, last week to protect them from possible defaults.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
